course: dictionary
lesson: 12618
title: Breaking apart: disintegrate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a thing coming apart. Disintegrate is one of them. Its two parts help: "dis" means apart, and "integrate" means joining together, so to disintegrate is to come apart from being whole. «The old paper began to disintegrate when Sam touched it.» Old paper that crumbles when touched is breaking into bits, so disintegrate means breaking into small pieces.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «The sandcastle slowly disintegrated when the tide came in.» Sandcastles crumble, and the tide washes them away, so disintegrated means fell apart into tiny pieces. Always test your meaning: put "fell apart into small pieces" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The word also works for things that are not solid. «The team began to disintegrate when everyone stopped talking.» Nothing broke into pieces here. The team became weaker and stopped working together, so disintegrate can also mean becoming weaker and stopping working as a whole.
fact: «Disintegrate» means to break into many small pieces and fall apart.
fact: «Disintegrate» can also mean to become weaker and stop working as a whole, like a team, plan or friendship.
fact: The verb forms are disintegrate, disintegrates, disintegrated and disintegrating.
fact: In science, rocks, meteors and old paper can disintegrate.
fact: Useful phrases are «disintegrate into pieces» and «slowly disintegrating».
exercise: «The rock began to disintegrate after years of rain and wind.» What does disintegrate mean here? | To be painted a new colour | To shine brightly | To grow bigger and stronger | *To break into small pieces
exercise: «The plan began to disintegrate when the team argued all day.» What does disintegrate suggest? | The plan was written in gold ink | The plan was finished early | The plan got better and better | *The plan became weaker and stopped working
exercise: «The old bridge was slowly disintegrating.» Find and copy the word that means breaking up slowly. | *disintegrating | was | slowly | bridge
test: «The meteor began to disintegrate as it burned through the sky.» What happened to the meteor? | It stopped moving and sat still | It grew into a planet | It landed softly on the grass | *It broke into pieces as it burned
test: «Ella's friendship began to disintegrate after the big argument.» What does disintegrate mean here? | *It became weaker and started to fall apart | It was sent by post | It became stronger and happier | It was made into a picture
exam: «The sandcastle slowly disintegrated when the tide came in.» What does disintegrated mean? | *It broke into tiny pieces and fell apart | It was painted red | It was cooked in the sun | It grew taller
